s://mfn.se/a/profoto/inbjudan-till-profotos-presentation-av-resultatet-for-det-andra-kvartalet-2026-den-17-juli-kl-09-00","tags":["ci","ci:other"]}],"events":[{"date":"2026-10-20","title":"Profoto's Interim Report January 1 – September 30, 2026","text":"Financial summary July – September 2026 * Net sales totaled SEK 128m (119), an increase of 7.9 percent. Organic growth was 7.7 percent, and the currency effect was 0.2 percent. * EBITDA amounted to SEK 40m (4) and the EBITDA margin to 30.9 percent (3.2). * EBIT amounted to SEK 19m (-57) and the EBIT margin to 14.6 percent (−47.9). * Earnings were positively impacted by a refund of U.S. tariffs of SEK 15m. * Profit for the period amounted to SEK 14m (−48). * Return on operating capital (LTM) was 9.5 percent (14.0). * Cash flow from operating activities amounted to SEK 25m (35). * Earnings per share (basic and diluted) amounted to SEK 0.36 (−1.19). Financial summary January – September 2026 * Net sales totaled SEK 419m (454), a decrease of 7.7 percent. Organic growth was -3.0 percent, and the currency effect was −4.7 percent. * EBITDA amounted to SEK 96m (71) and the EBITDA margin was 22.9 percent (15.7). * EBIT amounted to SEK 35m (−22) and the EBIT margin to 8.5 percent (−4.9). * Earnings were positively impacted by a refund of U.S. tariffs of SEK 15m. * Profit for the period amounted to SEK 26m (−30). * Cash flow from operating activities amounted to SEK 56m (113). * Earnings per share (basic and diluted) amounted to SEK 0.66 (−0.76). * Net debt amounted to SEK 151m (208), and the net debt/EBITDA LTM ratio was 1.17 (1.45). Sales growth with significant geographic variations: * Sales growth from low levels. * Improved earnings, partly due to a tariff refund. * Strengthened financial position. * LED-panel Profoto ProPanel is progressing as planned. – Anders Hedebark, CEO +------------+----------+----------+----------+----------+-----------+-------+ | | Jul–Sep | Jul–Sep | Jan–Sep | Jan–Sep | Oct | Full | | | 2026 | 20